11
01:16:23,333 --> 01:16:29,333
The Two Popes is a 2019 biographical drama film directed by Fernando Meirelles and written by Anthony
McCarten, adapted from McCarten's play The Pope which premiered at Royal & Derngate Theatre in 2019.

12
01:23:20,000 --> 01:23:26,000
Predominantly set in Vatican City in the aftermath of the Vatican leaks scandal, the film follows Pope Benedict XVI, played by Anthony Hopkins, as he attempts to convince Cardinal
Jorge Mario Bergoglio, played by Jonathan Pryce, to reconsider his decision to resign as an archbishop as he confides his own intentions to abdicate the papacy.

13
01:30:16,666 --> 01:30:22,666
The film premiered at the Telluride Film Festival on August 31, 2019.

14
01:37:13,333 --> 01:37:19,333
It began a limited theatrical release in the United States on November 27, 2019, and in the United
Kingdom on November 29, and started digital streaming on December 20, by Netflix.

15
01:44:10,000 --> 01:44:16,000
The performances of Pryce and Hopkins, as well as McCarten's screenplay, received high praise from critics, and all three
received nominations for their work at the Academy Awards, Golden Globes and British Academy Film Awards.

16
01:51:06,666 --> 01:51:12,666
The film explores themes of vatican (holy see), pope, based on
true story, catholic, roman catholic church.

17
01:58:03,333 --> 01:58:09,333
The tone is emotional.
